# Client (Next)

- Customer-facing **Valentia** Next.js app. Port defaults to 3000 (`npm run dev`).
- This is **not** the Next.js from training data — read `client/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next APIs (else official docs). Heed deprecation notices. Skill: `nextjs-16`.
- Talk to the shared Nest API (`server/`); do not invent a second domain backend.
- UI: follow [`design.md`](../../design.md); tokens only (no raw hex). Stack: `.cursor/rules/frontend-stack.mdc`.
- Prefer existing UI stack (shadcn / Tailwind / Phosphor).

## Skills

- Next/React: `nextjs-16`, `react-dev`, `react-useeffect`
- Forms / data / state / realtime: `form-validation`, `data-fetching`, `state-management`, `realtime-sockets`
- UI: `frontend-design`, `ui-ux-pro-max`
- API needs: `frontend-to-backend-requirements`
- Build/test: `implement`, `tdd`, `code-review`

Audit file changes under `releases/client.md` (see release-logging rule).
